 - `PromptLog.js` · `StoreFolder.js` — prompts of a session, and the folder one lives in.
 
+**Which URL a session lives at.** A session's page is at its folder's path, `/framework/ai/sessions/YYYY/MM/DD/<folder>/`, the same path where its `session.jsonl`, `page.jsonl` and task folders are saved, so the address bar and the disk agree. The folder name comes from the index (`session-<id8>`, or a Servex agent's own name), so it is unique and never changes when the session is renamed; the page shows the readable title. `StoreFolder.child()` reads line 1 of the folder's `session.jsonl` (`session` or `assign`), learns the id, and draws `AISessionDetail` there; real subfolders (task folders, a project folder such as `sessions-and-tasks/`) still route below it through `StoreFolder.route()`. The id URL `/framework/ai/sessions/<id>/` (uuid or agent id) is only a way in: `AISessionsPage.child()` looks up the folder (`AISessionDetail.folder_for`) and `route()` redirects there with `location.replace`, keeping `?search` and `#hash`. A session with no folder yet keeps its page at the id URL (no redirect, so no loop). Every link the site builds to a session goes through `AISession.page_url(id, fallback)`, which answers the folder path once the index has named the folder, else the fallback; the phone pages under `v/mobile/` keep their own routes.
+
 Watch out: a *Claude Code* session here is not [`ext/Session`](/framework/ext/Session/), the voice session. The old lowercase shims were retired to `ai/archive/retired/2026-10-13/sessions/`.
